# A block past `or.pred %p55, %p53, %p54; @%p55 bra` in tut_ll's
# annotated PTX under its record's grid: %p53 compares the CTA index,
# %p54 the warp index a shuffle broadcasts (`%r9 != 10`). The block runs
# where neither holds, so its threads are warp 10's lanes and its CTAs
# those where 128·%ctaid.x ≥ 1: the warp-index half of the condition is
# left to the warps shown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --ncu %fixtures/b200/tut_ll_BM128_BN128_w4_s2_wsTrue.attn_fwd.sm_100a.ncu.json %fixtures/b200/tut_ll_BM128_BN128_w4_s2_wsTrue.attn_fwd.sm_100a.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: {{^}}	elect.sync 	%r457|%p57, -1; // [<block 63>] <= warp 10 × lane * | CTAs 128·%ctaid.x ≥ 1 (1920/2048) | under line 2012 | exec ? (trips of $L__BB0_2){{$}}
